ing/t2 with body `owner=${OTHER}` \u2192 exits 2 (fail CLOSED; the body must not make it foreign). Case 'foreign': create pending/${OTHER}__t3 with body `owner=${MINE}` \u2192 exits 0 and the output names t3 as belonging to another session (match the exact foreign wording the existing ownership case asserts). Each case uses its own fresh project dir (shared fixture state fakes red \u2014 memory note).", "Red run: in scripts/lib/partition.sh, inside sentinel_owner_of_name (or scan_pending's per-entry owner lookup), temporarily prefer a body line: read the first line with `IFS= read -r _l < \"$path\"` and if it matches `owner=*` use `${_l#owner=}` as the owner. Run the suite alone \u2192 all three new cases FAIL (record which checks). If any passes under the mutation, the case is vacuous \u2014 fix the case, not the mutation.", "Restore: `git checkout -- scripts/lib/partition.sh` (the mutation is your own uncommitted edit on a file you did not otherwise change), then `git diff --quiet scripts/lib/partition.sh; echo $?` \u2192 0. Re-run the suite alone \u2192 0 failed.", "Raise FLOOR_SHELL in tests/floors.env by 3 (the spec's case count; the measured passed+skipped delta is \u22653 so the floor holds). Run `python3 scripts/validate_plugin.py` and `shellcheck tests/test-scripts.sh`. Commit tests/test-scripts.sh + tests/floors.env together; report baseline\u2192after counts and the red run's failing check names."]}

